note omega-mcp: state shared by every unit. Globals hold only what host words read or write
note directly (a global is never passed as an argument); request, tape, writer and reference data
note live in fn main's frame and travel as sized parameters.

note gv: scalar state cells, indexed by the g* constants below.
global gv ulong 64
note pk: packed argument list for execprog (u16 count, then u16 length + bytes per record).
global pk uchar 4096
note pa: path scratch; tdir: the per-call temporary directory path.
global pa uchar 4096
global tdir uchar 64
note sx: this executable; omcp: the pinned compiler; datp: the reference data directory.
global sx uchar 4096
global omcp uchar 4096
global datp uchar 4096
note cb: captured bytes. 0..32767 program stdout, 32768..40959 program stderr,
note 40960..45055 compiler stderr, 45056..110591 example source.
global cb uchar 131072
note wst: waitpid status; fds: pipefds output; sbuf: status record from the reaper.
global wst uchar 8
global fds uchar 8
global sbuf uchar 8
note inf: bwrap --info-fd text; lb: one server log line; rnd: random bytes; qb: decoded query.
global inf uchar 1024
global lb uchar 1024
global rnd uchar 16
global qb uchar 256
note bsha: a sha256 digest (the compiler at start-up, then each compiled binary); hbuf: discard buffer
note for unexpected status-pipe bytes.
global bsha uchar 32
global hbuf uchar 64

